=> Rapid vehicular braking produces strong horizontal acceleration, but it will not trigger false alarms if the following filters are applied:
- No Freefall: Braking does not produce the near-$0g$ weightlessness preceding a human fall.
- No Body Inversion: Sudden vehicular stops do not rotate the wearer's posture from vertical to horizontal relative to the gravity axis.
- Post-Braking Vibration: Vehicles continue vibrating with engine idle or passenger movement; human post-fall immobility yields a flatlined signal ($\sigma < 1.5 \text{ m/s}^2$).

